=== front matter ===
 
 
 
 
 
 

 

i  
 
Preface 
 
This is volume 10 of the 2013 Population and Housing Census. It shows the list of all settlements 
within districts across all the Local Government Areas at the time of the census enumeration. 
 
The directory of  settlements is one of the most disaggregated geographic presentations of the 
population of The Gambia. The mapping exercise precedes the census enumeration; mappers were 
deployed to the  entire country to  collect Global Positioning System (GPS) coordinates of 
residence, schools, h ealth facilities, places of worship, recreational centres, wells/taps etc.  In 
addition, the number of households and population of each residence in a settlement was collected. 
The mapping fi eld returns were us ed in ArcGIS (geographic information system software) to 
delineate and produce enumeration area (EA) maps which usually has about 500 people. The 
lists of the settlements were obtained from the Area Councils/Municipalities which were updated 
during the mapping exercise. One of  the problems encountered during the mapping exercise was 
some settlement names have changed. But this issue was resolved by asking the residents the 
original name of the settlement. 
 
In the report, all settlements at the time of the census were listed by sex, age group, LGA, district 
and settlement which can be used for planning purposes in cognisant of the need of the sectors. 
 
We thank Mr Baboucarr Daffeh, Ms Lolley Kah Jallow, Ms Sainabou Jasseh, Mr. Mohammed L. 
Janneh, Mr. Alagie Fanneh and Mr. Ebrima W. Manneh  for preparing this report. We also thank 
other GBoS staff for finalizing the report. 
 
We wish to extend sincere thanks to The Gambia government for providing funding for the conduct 
of the census, and the United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA) for their support both technical 
and financial for the conduct of the 2013 Population and Housing Census. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Nyakassi M.B. Sanyang 
 
Statistician General 

ii  
Introduction 
 
The definition of settlements are numerous and varied. In The Gambia, in Population and Housing 
Census undertakings, any settlement that meets the criteria below is regarded as a settlement. 
 
1.   A spatial entity within a specified locality that is occupied by a family or families. 
 
 
 
2.   A distinct cluster of buildings/structures in a locality identified by a name(s) used as a 
human settlement. 
 
The country is  divided into two Councils and five local administrative regions: Banjul City 
Council (BCC), Kanifing Municipal Council (KMC); West Coast Region (WCR), Lower River 
Region (LRR), North Bank Region (NBR), Central River Region (CRR) and Upper River Region 
(URR). The Gambia Bureau of Statistics uses Local Government Areas (LGAs) for purp oses of 
censuses and surveys.  These are Banjul (BCC), Kanifing (KMC), Brikama (WCR), Mansakonko 
(LRR), Kerewan (NBR), Kuntaur (CRR North), Janjangbureh (CRR South) and Basse (URR). A 
varying number of districts constitute an LGA except for Kanifing which has only one district. 
 
 
There are forty-four districts in The Gambia distributed as follows: Banjul (3), K anifing (1), 
Brikama ( 9), Mansakonko (6 ), K erewan (7 ), Kuntaur (5), Janjanbureh (6)  and Basse (7). As 
Kanifing is  the only LGA with one district which is Kanifing, the p rofile for the LGA only 
includes the LGA followed by the settlements. 
 
For s ettlement with two different names, the fi rst name is  stated and the alternate n ame is  in 
brackets. 
 
According to the results of the 2013 Population and Housing Census, the total number of settlements 
is 1891 as shown in table 1 below. 
 
